    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Invoices can now offer an early-payment discount, and the invoice page shows the reduced amount. `bin/e2e` passes: for the seeded $200 invoice with 5% off if paid within 10 days, it shows `$200.00` as the total and `$190.00` as the early-payment amount.\n\nThe request mentioned an OfficeFloor server, but this app is plain Spring Boot (as `CLAUDE.md` says), so I built the server side the Spring way.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V45__invoice_early_payment_discount.sql`, adds `early_payment_pct` and `early_payment_days` to `invoice`. Both default to 0, so existing invoices offer no discount.\n- **Server:**\n  - The invoice now stores the discount percentage and the number of days.\n  - The reduced amount is the invoice total less that percentage, rounded to the cent. The last day to pay is the issue date plus the number of days.\n  - The invoice details sent to the page now include the percentage, the days, the last day to pay and the reduced amount. The last two are empty when no discount is offered.\n  - There's a new endpoint, `PUT /api/projects/{projectId}/invoices/{invoiceId}/early-payment`, for setting the discount. Like the other discount and tax endpoints, it only works on drafts.\n  - The test seed endpoint accepts `earlyPaymentPct` and `earlyPaymentDays`.\n- **Front end:** on the invoice page:\n  - When a discount is offered, the totals table gets a row reading \"Pay by {date} (within N days) for X% off\", with the reduced amount in `invoice-early-pay-amount`.\n  - Draft invoices also get a form for setting the percentage and days, laid out like the existing discount, tax and levy forms.\n\n**Decisions you may want to change**\n- **Amount owed:** the discount doesn't change what's owed. The invoice still counts as PAID only when the full amount is paid, so a payment of $190 would leave it PARTIAL.\n- **What it's taken off:** the percentage comes off the full total including tax.\n- **When it shows:** the reduced amount appears only when both the percentage and the days are above zero. It also still appears after the pay-by date has passed.",
